    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d697">

                <pb facs="0723" n="619" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg619"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.00 Revolutions/71: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in El Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >McCafferty</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-01-26T19:00:00-06:00">January 26, 1932—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. At Legation’s suggestion destroyers <hi rendition="#italic">Wickes</hi> and
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Philip</hi> came to La Libertad today and the
                    commander is now in San Salvador. There has been a noticeable improvement in the
                    situation. The government forces have retaken Juayua, Izalco and the other towns
                    which were in the hands of the Communists.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">McCafferty</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
